{"status": "ok", "backend": "ddgs-auto", "query": "Protein elevation in small cell lung cancer: serum calcium levels and parathyroid hormone related protein", "retrieved_at": "2026-10-18T20:13:00.704980+00:00", "documents": [{"title": "Parathyroid hormone–related protein–mediated hypercalcemia of ...", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13585689/", "snippet": "Therefore, in malignancy, elevated PTHrP levels are thought to be closely related to the growth of the primary tumor and metastatic progression. This study aimed to clarify the clinical features of PTHrP-mediated hypercalcemia in patients with malignancy."}, {"title": "Hypercalcaemia in small cell lung cancer: Report of a case ...", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/095980499390304X", "snippet": "Jan 1, 1993 · We report a patient with extensive small cell cancer who presented with hypercalcaemia. Investigations suggested parathyroid hormone (PTH) receptor stimulation, although the serum PTH level was not elevated. PTH related protein (PTHrP) was localised in a biopsy specimen from the tumour."}, {"title": "First report of small cell lung cancer with PTHrP-induced ...Small-Cell Lung Cancer Presenting as Hypercalcemia - CureusHypercalcaemia in small cell lung cancer: Report of a case ...Parathyroid hormone-related protein (PTHrP) and malignancyParathyroid hormone-related protein measured at the time of ...", "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5638718/", "snippet": "Oct 10, 2017 · Here we report a patient diagnosed with small cell lung cancer after first presenting with parathyroid hormone-related peptide-induced hypercalcemic pancreatitis and developed walled-off necrosis that resulted in disruption of the main pancreatic duct. In contrast, it is rare in small-cell lung carcinoma (SCLC), where parathyroid hormone levels remain mostly within the normal range despite elevated calcium. We present a case of hypercalcemia in a patient with SCLC and discuss its clinical implications. Abstract Although hypercalcaemia is frequently associated with malignancy, it is very rare in small cell lung cancer despite the high incidence of lytic bone metastases. We report a patient with extensive small cell cancer who presented with hypercalcaemia. In comparison to the more insidious rise in calcium levels linked to the relatively slow rise and progression of PTH levels in primary hyperparathyroidism, MAH related PTHrP can cause a rapid and severe blood calcium elevation, with total levels that are often above 3 mmol/L. Oct 3, 2002 · Parathyroid hormone-related protein (PTH-rP) is a major cause of tumor-induced hypercalcemia (TIH) and frequently is found to be elevated in serum of patients with TIH."}]}
